# expect.stdout: 0\n
# expect.exit: 0
# expect.xfail: feature_coverage.py runs through bootstrap_general.sscript which does not yet wrap a `run CALL` in a retry loop when `useRetry CALL POLICY` attaches a policy. Direct semsc.py compilation works correctly (`python compiler/semsc.py THIS_FILE --emit-exe /tmp/x.exe && /tmp/x.exe` prints `0\n` because the retry loop runs the call 3 times until the counter walks from -3 to 0). Closing means teaching bootstrap_general to emit retry_top/body/inc/exit blocks around `run` when the call has a policy attached.
project UseRetryLoop
target console
runtime AgentRuntime 0.1
entry console main
error MainError
errorCase MainError CallFailed CallError
const oneStep I64 1
const negativeThreeStart I64 -3
storage module mutable retryProgressCounter I64 negativeThreeStart
retryPolicy fiveAttemptRetryPolicy
retryMaxAttempts fiveAttemptRetryPolicy 5
operation incrementAndReportProgress
input incrementAndReportProgress unusedTrigger I64
output incrementAndReportProgress I64
call incrementProgressCall math.addI64
arg incrementProgressCall left retryProgressCounter
arg incrementProgressCall right oneStep
run incrementProgressCall
bind nextProgressValue I64 incrementProgressCall
set module retryProgressCounter nextProgressValue
returnValue nextProgressValue
operation main
input main console Console
output main Result ExitCode MainError
effect main write console.stdout
memory main heap no
async main no
purpose main "useRetry retries while the call returns a negative value; counter walks -2 -> -1 -> 0; result of the successful attempt prints."
invariant main "Without retry, output would be -2 after a single attempt. With retry, the loop runs 3 times until the call returns 0 (not negative)."
label startMain
const zeroValue I64 0
useRetry retryHelperCall fiveAttemptRetryPolicy
call retryHelperCall incrementAndReportProgress
arg retryHelperCall unusedTrigger zeroValue
run retryHelperCall
bind finalProgressResult I64 retryHelperCall
call printResultCall console.writeIntegerLine
arg printResultCall console console
arg printResultCall value finalProgressResult
run printResultCall
ignoreOk printResultCall Void
const successfulExitCode ExitCode 0
returnOk successfulExitCode
